      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Gemma3MultiModalProjector` makes the vision output NCHW-contiguous before `avg_pool`. After `flatten(2).transpose(1, 2)` the pooled tokens are `[B, 256, hidden]` with `stride(-1) = 256`, so `mm_soft_emb_norm` gets a transposed input and the XPU path needs a copy before `gemma_rmsnorm` (#44225).\n\nThe view before that `.contiguous()` is already channels-last, since it comes from the token-major vision output. Pooling it directly keeps that layout, so the pooled tokens come out contiguous.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `models/gemma3_mm.py`: drop the `.contiguous()` before `avg_pool`.\n\nWith this, the `stride(-1) != 1` copy in `Gemma3RMSNorm.forward_xpu` (#44225) no longer triggers for Gemma-3.\n\n## Test\n\nPooled output vs the current code, for a `[B, 4096, 1152]` vision output:\n- Intel Arc Pro B60 and CPU, bf16/fp16/fp32: bit-equal, and now contiguous (`stride (294912, 1152, 1)`).\n- B60, bf16, B=8: pooling plus the copy for the norm, 660.6 µs → 377.8 µs.\n\nEnd-to-end accuracy run pending.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `pre-commit run` on the changed file: passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38810695865](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38810695865)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38810696129](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38810696129)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38810695787](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38810695787)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
